    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Question\n\nHello there.\r\n\r\nI work in a C codebase which uses block style comments.\r\n\r\nIf I try to comment a function with these, we get this duplicate comment issue which then breaks compilation. \r\n\r\nHere is an example\r\n\r\n```\r\nint func() {\r\n\t/* \r\n\t * is a block style comment\r\n\t */\r\n}\r\n\r\n/* int func() { */\r\n/* \t/*  */\r\n/* \t * is a block style comment */\r\n/* \t */ */\r\n/* } */\r\n``` \r\n\r\nFirst func is the defintion with, second is commented. \r\n\r\nI must admit, comments are one area of nvim I am not too familiar with, so maybe this is not a mini.comment issue? ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.comment</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello there.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I work in a C codebase which uses block style comments.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If I try to comment a function with these, we get this duplicate comment issue which then breaks compilation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is an example</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"int func() {\n\t/* \n\t * is a block style comment\n\t */\n}\n\n/* int func() { */\n/* \t/*  */\n/* \t * is a block style comment */\n/* \t */ */\n/* } */\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">int func() {\n\t/* \n\t * is a block style comment\n\t */\n}\n\n/* int func() { */\n/* \t/*  */\n/* \t * is a block style comment */\n/* \t */ */\n/* } */\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">First func is the defintion with, second is commented.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I must admit, comments are one area of nvim I am not too familiar with, so maybe this is not a mini.comment issue?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.comment\nQuestion\nHello there.\nI work in a C codebase which uses block style comments.\nIf I try to comment a function with these, we get this duplicate comment issue which then breaks compilation.\nHere is an example\nint func() {\n\t/* \n\t * is a block style comment\n\t */\n}\n\n/* int func() { */\n/* \t/*  */\n/* \t * is a block style comment */\n/* \t */ */\n/* } */\n\nFirst func is the defintion with, second is commented.\nI must admit, comments are one area of nvim I am not too familiar with, so maybe this is not a mini.comment issue?",
